# The `ui` stage installs its own with `npm ci`, and this keeps a workstation's
# copy from landing on top of it. The stage runs `RUN npm ci` and only THEN
# `COPY ui/ ./`, so without this line that second copy would overlay the
# laptop's node_modules over the freshly installed one — on a different platform
# (an arm64 mac building an amd64 image) that means native binaries built for
# the wrong architecture, in a tree that looks perfectly normal. Keeping several
# hundred megabytes out of the context upload is the secondary benefit.
ui/node_modules
# The local build output, which has no business in the context at all: the stage
# produces its own, and nothing in the image is ever copied from this directory.
#
# Correctness is already covered elsewhere — `emptyOutDir` in ui/vite.config.mjs
# wipes the directory before the stage writes into it, so a stale local dist
# cannot become the image's bundle. That is somebody else's setting, though, and
# this line keeps holding whatever it is set to next.
#
# What the line itself buys is the CONTEXT: ~140 KB rewritten by every local
# `make ui`, uploaded on every build to be used by nothing, and invalidating the
# `COPY ui/ ./` layer each time it changes.
#
# It does NOT protect the cache the split COPY above was arranged to keep. That
# one is `RUN npm ci`, and its layer sees only ui/package.json and
# ui/package-lock.json — ui/dist cannot reach it. `COPY ui/ ./` and
# `RUN npm run build` are invalidated by an edit to any component anyway, which
# is every ordinary iteration, so what this saves there is an upload rather than
# a rebuild.
ui/dist
# A workstation's `make ui` output, which `COPY static/ static/` would otherwise
# carry into the image — the same net as in .gitignore, deliberately wider than
# today's single file.
#
# The Dockerfile's copy ORDER is the other half of this and does not replace it.
# Order only settles a file the stage also emits, because winning means being
# copied over the same name; a chunk an older vite config produced and this build
# no longer does has nothing to overwrite it, so it would ship in the image as a
# file no commit can account for. That case is this line's alone.
static/_v/hammerola*
